From a55fd61686348cae6cb555fa53b4fb2d4ae7ca4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FLOOR Contributors <contributors@floor.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(floor-amm): add FloorAmm (the FLOOR Program) dex

One FloorAmm contract per chain, at the same address on every chain; every
launch (token vs its quote) trades against the contract itself from its
first block, so a pool is a launch id.

A launch's state is its book, read from the contract's launchBook view at
a block; any log of the launch re-reads it. Prices are the program's own
book walk (math/, a port of the protocol's reference math held to its
golden book walks bit for bit, testdata/book.json), exact-in both ways.
Each amount is priced as the contract fills it: a sell on its whole
10^-6-token units (sellFromBalance returns the rest to the recipient; under
one whole unit it is priced 0), and a buy filled whole but for a dust
refund (at most 1 ppm of the amount in, no step budget hit) at its tokens,
the dust going to refundTo. A larger refund, a budget hit or an unfilled
sell is priced 0, so the amount out is exactly what the recipient
receives. Liquidity is F + C + K + the money in place, in USD.
